#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:491
#: 9b2f16060af2447ba811b1aadf1ff1fe
msgid "Mini FAQ"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:492
#: bf38ed0cc5bb4590aef7d7db6c1b8cb7
msgid ""
"**Do I need EMBED_PROVIDER/EMBED_MODEL?** You only need "
"EMBED_PROVIDER/EMBED_MODEL for building collections or for "
"embedding/hybrid search. ``keyword`` search and ``sync-hf`` do **not** "
"require an embedding provider/model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:494
#: 260c723de8d9446f87ff2dcf1734ceab
msgid ""
"**What’s “hybrid” search?** A smart mix of exact words + meaning. Start "
"here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:496
#: b7557e9501df44099ae7c0143b3d3994
msgid ""
"**Do I need to set an embedding dimension?** No — it’s detected "
"automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:498
#: baf73e0847d3457cb159ab3bd1f96678
msgid "**Changed models?** Rebuild; dimensions are auto-handled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:500
#: 37fb2f9974e14466a1956329fc60e03f
msgid ""
"**Re-running build?** Safe. Duplicates (same ``doc_key``) are ignored; "
"new text is added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:502
#: 17a0d29ef9b44e7e97604b32d805f23b
msgid ""
"**“No results”?** Try ``--method keyword`` or confirm the "
"``--collection`` name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:504
#: ab85b05705794c15943f6b9d40ff5fad
msgid ""
"**Where are my searchable datasets stored locally?** "
"``<user_cache_dir>/embeddings/``. Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:505
#: 214b041c3c214e22bd488963faa871f7
msgid "macOS → ``~/Library/Caches/ToolUniverse``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:506
#: 7ddb9185f64e4bcfbcccbf054d3938e0
msgid "Linux → ``~/.cache/tooluniverse``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:507
#: 93f88cae7317467f8553d39d17aa28d5
msgid "Windows → ``%LOCALAPPDATA%\\\\ToolUniverse``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:509
#: 0ab73537725a42e997b76fbe5c4d2886
msgid "**Where do my tools live?**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:510
#: 3bb0de7dd4c64866b4d4d7db49ce12c7
msgid "``~/.tooluniverse/data/user_tools/`` (auto-loaded)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:512
#: cd3b1192a5a14b1fa7ef1c4395959a46
msgid ""
"**Where does my data upload?** ``tu-datastore sync-hf upload`` targets "
"your **own** HF account by default (based on your token)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:514
#: f00a26b7eeaa4496a3650789af64ded3
msgid "**What is the`EmbeddingCollectionSearchTool`?**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:515
#: ad789b0abb1342b4a4b4302379b4e145
msgid ""
"-`EmbeddingCollectionSearchTool` is a **real ToolUniverse tool** "
"(registered in code). Check "
"``src/tooluniverse/database_setup/generic_embedding_search_tool.py`` for "
"details. - We don’t ship a pre-bound JSON for it because the collection "
"name is yours. - Use the example JSON under ``docs/tools/``, set "
"``\"fields.collection\"`` to your collection (e.g., "
"``\"cardiology_tutorial\"``), and load it - If you prefer not to create a"
" JSON, you can also instantiate the tool directly from Python and pass "
"the collection name via ``fields``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:520
#: f264ce9f4c4141539e31dc3382f639df
msgid ""
"**Can I upload my tool with the datastore?** Yes, pass one or more files "
"via ``--tool-json`` during ``sync-hf upload``; they’re stored at the "
"dataset root."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:522
#: dba20d0ade1349bc9ef42d1611fc91af
msgid ""
"**How do I pull tool JSONs too?** Use ``--include-tools`` with ``sync-hf "
"download`` to download any ``*.json`` in the dataset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:524
#: 9af00dcdb44e44e4a39f6afeea4cad68
msgid ""
"**Is upload private by default?** Yes auto upload **private** datasets "
"unless you opt out (CLI: ``--no-private``; tool: set ``\"private\": "
"false``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:526
#: c21ed5cbd96248e585055a400383950e
msgid "**Do I have to pass --db to search/build?**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:527
#: a7a01d5bafeb42fd8d97c3236187d140
msgid "No — both commands write and read from your cache automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:528
#: e17b4455eef94fa1bc2cfb3e4409d0eb
msgid ""
"Use `--db` only if you want a **custom output path** (for example, a "
"shared directory)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:529
#: 612ecc4df8dc4d8fbe85eb74002d9165
msgid ""
"When using the **JSON tool** or agents, no paths are ever needed — "
"everything resolves automatically from the collection name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:531
#: 9e0d37ae6bf246deb89cd5d3049e3439
msgid ""
"**When building my custom datastore what if I want to use different "
"provider(s) and/or model(s) for my embeddings?** You can use a different "
"provider/model when building your searchable datastore like we do in the "
"example below — just make sure that if you want to keep the initial "
"provider/model based datastore, you give this new build's collection a "
"new name or else it will override the initial build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/make_your_data_agent_searchable.rst:537
#: 8646e0c4d39b4729949fb4ade1d3a50e
msgid ""
"**Can I have JSON files in a folder I use with 'quickbuild'?** "
"`quickbuild` does **not** read JSON files in a folder; use `build --docs-"
"json` for JSON ingestion."
msgstr ""

